---
Run a Wasm module locally against the in-process TensorWasm engine

Usage: tensor-wasm run [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          Path to the `.wasm` file to execute

Options:
      --export <EXPORT>
          Name of the exported function to call. Defaults to `main`
          
          [default: main]

      --tenant <TENANT>
          Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests via `X-TensorWasm-Tenant`. Zero (the default) suppresses the header for backwards compatibility
          
          [default: 0]

      --args <ARGS>
          Arguments to pass to the export, encoded as a JSON array.
          
          Example: `--args '[1.0, 2.0]'`. The current executor only invokes `() -> ()` exports, so the array is parsed and validated but the values are not yet wired into the call site.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
